  "id": "DrugBank_DB00997 - MONDO_3792",
  "verbalization": "Doxorubicin appears to have a potential role in the treatment of ovarian carcinosarcoma through a multi-step pathway involving different subtypes of ovarian cancer. The evidence suggests that Doxorubicin is linked to Ovarian Carcinosarcoma via its ability to induce the progression of various ovarian malignancies, including Ovarian Clear Cell Adenocarcinoma and Malignant Germ Cell Tumor Of Ovary. These subtypes, in turn, are associated with Carboplatin, which is indicated for their treatment. The presence of a direct indication from Doxorubicin to Ovarian Carcinosarcoma, through these intermediate entities, implies a possible mechanism of action that involves chemotherapy or drug synergy in the context of ovarian cancer. The integration of these pathways highlights the complex interplay between Doxorubicin and ovarian malignancies, suggesting that its use may be relevant in the management of certain subtypes of ovarian carcinosarcoma.",
